  },
  {
    "summary": "The **Kanban Method** is guided by **Foundational Principles** that emphasize starting with the current process (\"Start with what you do now\"), pursuing gradual improvements (\"Agree to pursue evolutionary change\"), respecting existing organizational structures (\"Initially, respect current roles, responsibilities & job titles\"), and fostering initiative (\"Encourage acts of leadership at all levels\").",
    "source_indices": [2, 3, 4, 5]
  },
  {
    "summary": "The **Kanban Method** employs several **Core Practices** to optimize workflow: \"Visualize\" makes the workflow transparent (e.g., using a Kanban board); \"Limit WIP\" (**Work In Progress**) reduces multitasking and identifies constraints; \"Manage flow\" optimizes work item movement; \"Make policies explicit\" defines clear rules; \"Implement feedback loops\" enables continuous adaptation; and \"Improve collaboratively, evolve experimentally (using models and the scientific method)\" promotes data-driven, collective improvement.",
    "source_indices": [6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11]
  },
  {
    "summary": "The curriculum for all **LeanKanban University Certified Kanban Training** classes is based on the Kanban Method, and its principles and practices are followed by all **LKU Kanban Coaching Professionals**, ensuring a standardized approach to teaching and applying the method.",
